[size=3][b]Foreword[/b][/size]
The New Gentleman (TNG) has evolved over time and so much has changed since its initial release. In this article, I will try to summarize the evolution of TNG between major versions. The purpose is to have a documentation of what worked and what failed in the past, the mechanics behind TNG, the reasoning behind design decisions, and how we arrived at the current state of TNG. This article is mainly for those who wants to understand TNG better and possibly contribute to its development in the future. If you are just a user of TNG and want to know how to use it, you can skip this article and read the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/50266]main TNG mod page[/url] and the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/50266?tab=articles]articles[/url] instead.

[size=3][b]Before the release of version 1.0: The Prototype[/b][/size]
TNG started as a mod to replace [url=https://www.loverslab.com/files/file/5355-schlongs-of-skyrim-se/]Schlongs of Skyrim SE[/url][i](adult website)[/i] and utilize engine developments and newer possibilities in Skyrim SE/AE. The idea and the main design principles were: [list]
[*]having a good quality body mesh, texture, animations, and genitalia control mechanism are provided out of the box,
[*]the body resembling vanilla body in shape, so that no refitting is required for armors and clothes,
[*]avoid using scripts and affecting save file so that the mod could be installed/uninstalled/updated easily without breaking saves,
[*]providing compatibility with all animations that worked with SOS and SoS-based mods,
[*]providing a framework for modders to create addons for TNG easily or convert the existing SOS addons to TNG addons,
[*]ensuring compatibility with texture(skin) and mesh overhauls designed for SOS.
[/list]
This could be achieved by modifying the skin of races to include the genitalia armor addons when you launch the game, before the main menu appears. 
